{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["# Velnor Model Training in Google Colab\n","\n","This notebook clones the `velnor` repository, sets up the build environment, compiles the kernel, and runs a QEMU emulation to simulate training‑like execution. It also includes a second part that fine‑tunes a 3.8 B LLM (e.g., Qwen‑3.8B) with LoRA on the Velnor curriculum. Adjust the steps as needed for actual model training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "install-deps"},
      "source": ["# System packages for building Velnor\n","!apt-get update -y && apt-get install -y build-essential qemu-system-x86 clang llvm git python3-pip\n",
      "# Python packages for LLM fine‑tuning (GPU enabled)\n",
      "!pip install -q "
      "torch torchvision torchaudio --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118 && \
      "pip install -q transformers datasets peft accelerate tqdm huggingface_hub\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "clone-repo"},
      "source": ["# Clone Velnor repository\n","!git clone https://github.com/vectolith/velnor.git\n",
      "%cd velnor\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "build-velnor"},
      "source": ["# Build the Velnor project (uses the repository's Makefile)\n","!make clean && make -j$(nproc)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "run-qemu"},
      "source": ["# Run QEMU in headless mode and capture serial output\n",
        "!qemu-system-x86_64 -drive format=raw,file=out/kernel.bin -nographic -serial file:serial.log &\n",
        "import time, os\n",
        "time.sleep(30)  # Let the VM boot for ~30 seconds\n",
        "!cat serial.log | tail -n 20\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["## Fine‑tune a 3.8 B LLM with Velnor curriculum\n","The following cells use the `transformers` + `peft` stack to fine‑tune a 3.8 B model (e.g., `Qwen/Qwen2.5-3.8B-Instruct`). Adjust `BASE_MODEL` and LoRA hyper‑parameters as required."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "setup‑llm"},
      "source": ["BASE_MODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-3.8B-Instruct\"  # or any compatible 3.8B checkpoint\n",
        "from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n",
        "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(BASE_MODEL, torch_dtype='auto', device_map='auto')\n",
        "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(BASE_MODEL, trust_remote_code=True)\n",
        "tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "prepare‑data"},
      "source": ["# Load the Velnor curriculum JSONL (generated in the repo)\n",
        "import json, pathlib\n",
        "data_path = pathlib.Path('training/general_curriculum.jsonl')\n",
        "samples = []\n",
        "with data_path.open() as f:\n",
        "    for line in f:\n",
        "        obj = json.loads(line)\n",
        "        # Simple chat‑like format for PEFT\n",
        "        prompt = obj.get('prompt', '')\n",
        "        completion = obj.get('completion', '')\n",
        "        samples.append({\"input\": prompt, \"output\": completion})\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to a HuggingFace Dataset\n",
        "from datasets import Dataset\n",
        "dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\"text\": [s['input'] + tokenizer.eos_token + s['output'] for s in samples]})\n",
        "# Tokenize\n",
        "def tokenize_fn(ex):\n",
        "    return tokenizer(ex['text'], truncation=True, max_length=1024)\n",
        "tokenized = dataset.map(tokenize_fn, batched=False)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"id": "train‑lora"},
      "source": ["from peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model\n",
        "# LoRA hyper‑parameters – feel free to tweak\n",
        "lora_cfg = LoraConfig(\n",
        "    r=64,\n",
        "    lora_alpha=32,\n",
        "    target_modules=['q_proj','v_proj','k_proj','o_proj'],\n",
        "    lora_dropout=0.1,\n",
        "    bias='none',\n",
        "    task_type='CAUSAL_LM'\n",
        ")\n",
        "model = get_peft_model(model, lora_cfg)\n",
        "model.print_trainable_parameters()\n",
        "\n",
        "from transformers import Trainer, TrainingArguments\n",
        "training_args = TrainingArguments(\n",
        "    output_dir='lora-velnor',\n",
        "    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n",
        "    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n",
        "    learning_rate=3e-4,\n",
        "    num_train_epochs=3,\n",
        "    fp16=True,\n",
        "    logging_steps=10,\n",
        "    save_strategy='epoch'\n",
        ")\n",
        "trainer = Trainer(\n",
        "    model=model,\n",
        "    args=training_args,\n",
        "    train_dataset=tokenized\n",
        ")\n",
        "trainer.train()\n",
        "trainer.save_model('lora-velnor-final')\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["### After training\n",
        "* The LoRA adapters are saved in `lora-velnor-final/`.\n",
        "* You can download them from the Colab file browser or `!zip -r lora-velnor-final.zip lora-velnor-final` and then `files.download`.\n",
        "* To inference, load the base model and apply `PeftModel.from_pretrained`.\n"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {"kernelspec": {"display_name": "Python 3", "language": "python", "name": "python3"}, "language_info": {"name": "python", "version": "3.x"}},
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5
}
